KG42.register("rules-23c6b9d03e994220e8321ba5",{"id":"30-motivational_game::v141-c-R005","paper":"30-motivational_game","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R005","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Prosumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"The P2P trading price must always encourage prosumers to participate. Scope: Participation incentives for the canonical coalition game's community P2P trading scheme. P2P trading is expected to be conducted exclusively by network prosumers, with negligible grid influence. Scope: Expected participant composition of the described P2P energy networks. Prosumers need to participate continuously. Scope: Sustainable operation of P2P trading within an energy system. Condition: To ensure sustainable P2P trading operation.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.prosumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.prosumer","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"participation.prosumer","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Expected participant composition of the described P2P energy networks. | Participation incentives for the canonical coalition game's community P2P trading scheme. | Sustainable operation of P2P trading within an energy system.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g03-e002"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The P2P trading price must always encourage prosumers to participate. Scope: Participation incentives for the canonical coalition game's community P2P trading scheme.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"P2P trading is expected to be conducted exclusively by network prosumers, with negligible grid influence. Scope: Expected participant composition of the described P2P energy networks.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Prosumers need to participate continuously. Scope: Sustainable operation of P2P trading within an energy system. Condition: To ensure sustainable P2P trading operation.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e002"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-dd42379cd7-p01-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"Abstract","anchor_text":"T Thomas Morstync, Malcolm D. McCullochc, rgy trading. provided. nergy networks is expected to be ex","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"Peer-to-peer trading in energy networks is expected to be exclusively conducted by the prosumers of the network with negligible influence from the grid. This raises the critical question: how can enough prosumers be encouraged to participate in peer-to-peer trading so as to make its operation sustainable and beneficial to the overall electricity network?"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-dd42379cd7-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2.1 Stability of a coalition; Definition 2","anchor_text":"The stability of a canonical coalition game refers to the fact that the w grand coalition2 is stable","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The stability of a canonical coalition game refers to the fact that the grand coalition2 is stable. That means once the grand coalition of prosumers is formed for P2P trading, no prosumer will have an incentive to leave the grand coalition for further improving its benefit. Mathematically, a grand coalition is stable if (1) it has a non-empty core, which is a vector of revenue allocation that ensures that each prosumer that forms a coalition with other prosumers for trading energy receives a revenue such that it has no incentive to leave the grand coalition [56], and (2) the revenue that each prosumer will achieve for participating in P2P trading always lie within the core [56].\nDefinition 2. From a coalition game perspective, peer-to-peer energy trading between the prosumers will be stable if:\n• The game possesses a non-empty core, that is, the value function of the coalition needs to be superadditive. For the definition of core and superadditivity, please see [56].\n• The P2P energy trading price needs to ensure that the revenue that each prosumer may attain lies within the core [56]. In other words, the P2P trading price needs to always encourage the prosumers to participate."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e002","location":{"location_id":"src-dd42379cd7-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4. Conclusion","anchor_text":"motivational psychology models has been demonstrated, and thus, its potential to enable widespread p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"• To ensure a sustainable operation of peer-to-peer trading within an energy system, prosumers need to participate continuously. Hence, motivating them to participate is an important part of the design of a peer-to-peer trading scheme.\n• Motivational psychology provides a number of models, which, with a suitable application, has proven to be eﬀective in other domains for motivating people to work towards achieving particular objectives. These models can be exploited to design a peer-to-peer trading scheme in order to ensure prosumers’ sustainable participation."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No source-defined decision variable is introduced in the frozen rule's attached evidence. The quoted participation requirement refers generically to a P2P trading price and prosumer participation without defining a symbol or domain for this rule; declaring p_s/p_b here would reuse price-formation symbols outside this rule's explicit source scope.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed numeric parameter, threshold, or price value is stated for encouraging participation. The core and superadditivity requirements are referred to cited sources rather than supplied as parameters, and the grid-price values are outside this rule's frozen members."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-validation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.prosumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","quote":"In other words, the P2P trading price needs to always encourage the prosumers to participate."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E01","quote":"Peer-to-peer trading in energy networks is expected to be exclusively conducted by the prosumers of the network with negligible influence from the grid."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e002","quote":"To ensure a sustainable operation of peer-to-peer trading within an energy system, prosumers need to participate continuously."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"dd4b4c1325df60955710863b1a7de3058da404dc3c98e02148143f39a6c65af7","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"The supplied source supports qualitative participation requirements, but the one mathematical stability condition tied to this rule states that the P2P trading price must ensure each prosumer's attainable revenue lies within the game's core. The frozen graph contains only pricing.local and participation.prosumer with one links edge; it has no core, revenue-allocation, superadditivity, or per-prosumer revenue entity. Therefore the existing procedural constraints are retained as not_formalized, and a source-faithful expression cannot be written without inventing missing entities or symbols. The supplied evidence remains unreviewed under the experiment policy.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","node_ids":["pricing.local","participation.prosumer"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R005-E001"],"rationale":"C001 is represented by the frozen pricing.local -> participation.prosumer links edge; the source statement is qualitative and supplies no explicit price-to-participation formula for the current graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","node_ids":["participation.prosumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 concerns participant composition only; the frozen graph contains participation.prosumer but no dedicated grid-influence or admission edge for this procedural scope statement."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C003","node_ids":["participation.prosumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C003 concerns continuous prosumer participation for sustainability; the frozen graph contains participation.prosumer but no separate continuity or sustainability edge."}],"revision_requests":["C.1: add a source-scoped validation/core-stability entity and, if Definition 2 is to be represented, an edge from pricing.local to that entity; the frozen graph currently has no core, revenue-allocation, or superadditivity node.","C.1: if a quantitative participation-pricing constraint is intended, provide exact source-scoped symbols and domains for the P2P trading price(s) and each prosumer's attainable revenue, rather than inferring or cross-rule reusing price symbols.","C.1: clarify whether participant composition (C002) and continuous participation (C003) require dedicated graph relations or are intentionally represented only by participation.prosumer context."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
